lctech f1c200s: enable the on-chip audio codec (headphone + speaker, mic)

The suniv codec driver (CONFIG_SND_SUN4I_CODEC=y) and its DMA engine are
already built, but the mainline dtsi leaves codec@1c23c00 disabled, so the
board booted with "No soundcards found". Enable it with the routing proven
on mainline's LicheePi Nano (same SoC): Headphone <- HP/HPCOM, MIC <- Mic,
plus Speaker <- HP for the board's PAM8301 amplifier (always on; no enable
GPIO, so no allwinner,pa-gpios). FastCarPlay plays through SDL's ALSA
backend on the "default" device, which is this card.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/suniv-f1c200s-lctech-pi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/suniv-f1c200s-lctech-pi.dts
@@ -398,3 +398,20 @@
 		status = "okay";
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * On-chip audio codec (sun4i-codec, suniv variant). The board brings out the
+ * headphone pair HPL/HPR (AC-coupled, R3/R4 + 1 uF) -- which also feeds the
+ * on-board PAM8301 speaker amplifier (always on, no enable GPIO) -- and MICIN.
+ * Routing mirrors mainline's LicheePi Nano (same SoC) plus the speaker sink.
+ * No pinmux: these are dedicated analog pins. The codec's DMA channels are
+ * already declared in the suniv dtsi (DMA_SUN4I).
+ */
+&codec {
+	allwinner,audio-routing =
+		"Headphone", "HP",
+		"Headphone", "HPCOM",
+		"Speaker", "HP",
+		"MIC", "Mic";
+	status = "okay";
+};
